<h3>2. Refund vs. Carry-Forward</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Carry-forward (default):</b> credit nets against Q1 invoices automatically; no action needed</li>
<li><b>Cash refund:</b> requires a bank authorization form on file — refund wired within 10 business
days of quarter close</li>
<li>Historically ~60% of clients carry forward; refund suits those reducing scope in Q1</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Bank Authorization Form</h3>
<p>The refund wire requires an authorized remittance target. The governance portal's form collects:
beneficiary name, account number, SWIFT/routing, an <b>authorized-signatory specimen</b> (photo or scan
of a wet or electronic signature matching your MSA signatory card), and the account holder's phone number
with an SMS confirmation code. Once submitted, the form covers all future credits for the MSA term —
you won't repeat it per quarter.</p>

