<h3>4. Timeline</h3>
<ul>
<li>Bank authorization deadline: <b>before the quarter close (calendar month end)</b></li>
<li>Refund wire: within 10 business days after close</li>
<li>After close: credit irrevocably applies to Q1 invoices</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px">A service provider emailing you a form that
collects bank details plus a signature specimen is exactly what fraud training warns about — and we
know it. Controls here: the form is scoped to credit memo CM-88417 (the memo number appears on every
page, and the portal shows the same breach table your monthly SLA reports contain); the form never
asks for passwords, tokens, or card data; and your account team can confirm the determination on your
regular governance call before you act. The quarter-close date, however, is the finance calendar's,
not ours.</p>

